WEBVTT

01:35.570 --> 01:39.620
EPISODE 9: THE RULER OF RELICS

01:39.620 --> 01:44.560
Silver Axe! Blow away the enemy before me!

01:52.340 --> 01:53.880
What the hell?!

01:54.410 --> 01:57.260
This is humiliating, you villain!

01:54.840 --> 01:56.770
Show your true form, relic.

01:59.850 --> 02:02.680
Well, that's a damn fine sword.

02:06.360 --> 02:09.360
THE VALIANT PIRATE'S SWORD 
BESTOWED BY THE KING
(GRADE A - EPIC / CONSUMABLE RELIC)
USES: (2,594/5,000)

02:06.670 --> 02:08.630
A pirate's sword, huh?

02:09.360 --> 02:10.900
What's taking him so long?

02:10.900 --> 02:13.220
You think something happened?

02:19.640 --> 02:21.710
Jump in, Boss!

02:22.990 --> 02:25.800
Later! I'll be sure to use this!

02:27.500 --> 02:31.280
Hey! Stop! Give me back my relic!

02:36.950 --> 02:39.960
You bastard! Just you wait!

02:38.040 --> 02:39.560
They're all yours!

02:55.240 --> 02:58.260
There it is. Bring the boat 
over to that big tree.

02:58.260 --> 02:59.120
Got it.

03:05.250 --> 03:09.250
Spreading that foul relic stench 
all the way out here...

03:09.660 --> 03:11.420
You're awfully bold.

03:13.130 --> 03:15.940
You actually found me.

03:15.940 --> 03:18.150
I acknowledge your abilities.

03:18.150 --> 03:21.960
However, to obtain my power, 
you must offer a sacred prayer.

03:21.960 --> 03:25.020
Just try and satisfy me.

03:25.400 --> 03:27.020
Don't make me laugh.

03:27.370 --> 03:28.930
What?

03:29.520 --> 03:34.150
I don't make friends with relics.

03:37.090 --> 03:39.160
What do you think you're doing?!

03:44.920 --> 03:47.320
Impossible...

03:55.590 --> 03:58.680
MAP OF ZHENG HE'S TREASURES OF THE WEST
(GRADE A - EPIC / CONSUMABLE RELIC)
USES: (2/500)

03:58.680 --> 04:01.680
Zheng He's Treasures of the West, huh?

04:01.680 --> 04:03.180
"Zheng He"?

04:03.470 --> 04:08.140
Zheng He was sent by the emperor 
on a voyage to the southern seas.

04:08.660 --> 04:10.250
This map was essential

04:10.250 --> 04:13.420
for finding all the treasures in the sea.

04:14.150 --> 04:17.660
Cutting down the whole tree 
cost it some durability.

04:17.660 --> 04:19.960
Restore this, too, while you're at it.

04:20.530 --> 04:23.530
Be more careful with these things!

04:30.960 --> 04:36.450
I gave Edward the fake map, like you said,
but isn't this way too dangerous?

04:36.970 --> 04:39.450
We're dealing with 
General Kiera Clark, after all.

04:40.260 --> 04:43.970
It'll be fine. Irene-san, 
put your hand on the map.

04:44.510 --> 04:46.760
Oh, um... All right.

04:49.800 --> 04:55.330
Show us everything connected 
to this misfortune relic.

05:02.920 --> 05:04.440
Turkey.

05:05.000 --> 05:08.160
That's exactly why we needed this map.

05:08.160 --> 05:11.500
We'll have to go there 
to solve your problem.

05:11.940 --> 05:14.080
This map will still come in handy.

05:14.780 --> 05:16.010
I see.

05:16.550 --> 05:19.770
Kiera is collecting all the map relics,

05:19.770 --> 05:22.510
so she probably has 
Columbus's Map, as well.

05:22.510 --> 05:26.170
It shows where tombs are 
and what relics are in them.

05:27.220 --> 05:32.020
She's probably using it to monitor 
every relic site in the world.

05:34.560 --> 05:37.240
Flying to Turkey now 
would be too dangerous.

05:37.820 --> 05:39.910
Then what do we do?

05:41.420 --> 05:44.740
We destroy every map 
relic in Kiera's possession.

05:46.820 --> 05:48.740
That's... all?

05:48.740 --> 05:53.330
Unbelievable! There's 
something wrong with you!

05:54.150 --> 05:57.790
Did you forget that the fake 
will disappear in time?

05:57.790 --> 06:02.010
We should start running right now!
What are you thinking?!

06:02.340 --> 06:03.510
I know a way.

06:03.510 --> 06:04.640
You do?

06:06.670 --> 06:09.180
Goriki Ryoga, you damn fraud!

06:10.270 --> 06:12.770
What did you give me?!

06:12.770 --> 06:16.560
Hey, what's all this about, Edward? 
Just calm down.

06:16.560 --> 06:19.190
The relic you gave me disappeared.

06:19.190 --> 06:21.780
The general is furious and wants my head.

06:21.780 --> 06:25.290
It disappeared? Please, tell me more.

06:25.650 --> 06:29.790
It just suddenly vanished 
while the general was using it!

06:30.170 --> 06:33.040
See? Sounds like it was working just fine.

06:33.040 --> 06:35.470
I would never give you a fake.

06:35.470 --> 06:37.750
Could she have destroyed 
the relic by accident?

06:37.750 --> 06:38.680
What?

06:39.160 --> 06:43.100
<i>The copies can imitate the 
originals to a certain degree.</i>

06:43.460 --> 06:47.470
Then... it wasn't a fake?

06:48.740 --> 06:50.840
What on earth happened?

06:50.840 --> 06:54.090
That doesn't explain why 
the relic disappeared

06:54.090 --> 06:58.200
or why everyone who was nearby 
at the time vanished along with it.

06:58.200 --> 07:00.820
Including the British prime minister.

07:01.300 --> 07:04.360
What?! Why was he there?

07:04.670 --> 07:07.870
Apparently, he was secretly
meeting with the general.

07:07.870 --> 07:10.840
This could lead to war.

07:11.880 --> 07:13.370
What do we do now, Boss?

07:13.370 --> 07:16.370
<i>Perfect. This is my chance.</i>

07:16.770 --> 07:20.880
Hey, Edward, why don't 
you let me talk to Kiera?

07:20.880 --> 07:24.260
What? T-To the general?

07:32.330 --> 07:34.590
<i>Hello, General.</i>

07:35.210 --> 07:38.740
<i>It's a pleasure to meet you. 
My name is Goriki Ryoga.</i>

07:38.740 --> 07:43.130
Likewise. Though I had imagined 
our first conversation differently.

07:43.130 --> 07:46.490
I hear you overpowered my 
people and stole their relics.

07:46.750 --> 07:50.150
And now there's a problem with 
the relic you delivered to me.

07:50.150 --> 07:52.990
I'll need to hold you 
responsible for that.

07:53.270 --> 07:57.500
Tell me the truth if you want to live. 
What did you do to that relic?

07:57.500 --> 07:59.670
Absolutely nothing.

07:59.670 --> 08:03.000
I merely handed the relic over to Edward.

08:03.000 --> 08:05.510
GENERAL KIERA CLARK

08:03.000 --> 08:05.510
<i>And you expect me to believe that?</i>

08:05.510 --> 08:09.350
I understand your doubts. 
That's why I called.

08:09.350 --> 08:12.050
I hear the British prime minister 
disappeared, as well.

08:12.050 --> 08:14.760
Since this problem arose 
from our transaction,

08:14.760 --> 08:18.020
I'd like to help as part of my service.

08:18.490 --> 08:23.520
As part of your service, you intend 
to find the British prime minister?

08:23.520 --> 08:28.690
Edward told me that you 
possess several map relics.

08:29.660 --> 08:34.340
Unfortunately, none of them have 
the power to locate a person.

08:34.740 --> 08:38.450
Many believe relics only possess 
their predetermined functions.

08:38.450 --> 08:40.120
That is not the case.

08:40.440 --> 08:43.730
I know how to draw out 
a relic's full potential,

08:43.730 --> 08:48.630
maximize its abilities, 
and even create new ones.

08:48.630 --> 08:50.130
SERIOUSLY?

08:48.630 --> 08:50.130
<i>Seriously?</i>

08:50.130 --> 08:52.390
NOPE.

08:50.130 --> 08:51.840
<i>Obviously not.</i>

08:52.810 --> 08:56.890
New abilities? And that's possible?

08:57.400 --> 09:02.020
That's the only reason 
I managed to shake off the CIA.

09:04.910 --> 09:06.140
Very well.

09:11.300 --> 09:14.490
Well? Do you think you can convince her?

09:15.730 --> 09:18.000
Piece of cake.

09:25.630 --> 09:29.010
Wow, this is one fancy hotel.

09:29.440 --> 09:32.510
No less than expected from 
someone like Kiera Clark.

09:32.810 --> 09:34.430
May I help you?

09:36.070 --> 09:40.150
She's concerned because you were 
walking around with that spaced-out look.

09:40.150 --> 09:42.770
Thank you, but that 
won't be necessary, Jamie.

09:43.770 --> 09:46.110
Oh, I saw your name tag.

09:49.650 --> 09:51.650
Are you Goriki Ryoga?

09:52.080 --> 09:53.160
Yes.

09:53.710 --> 09:54.750
Thank you, Jamie.

09:54.750 --> 09:55.750
Of course.

10:17.470 --> 10:19.750
Welcome, Goriki.

10:22.140 --> 10:24.690
<i>So this is Kiera Clark.</i>

10:25.560 --> 10:28.300
She's pretty young for a general.

10:28.300 --> 10:29.680
Where are the maps?

10:32.320 --> 10:35.570
You're just as insolent as they say.
Follow me.

10:42.640 --> 10:46.700
<i>There's the A-grade Columbus's Map relic.</i>

10:46.700 --> 10:49.480
<i>And B- and C-grade relics, too.</i>

10:50.570 --> 10:54.470
Well, show me your magnificent skill.

10:54.470 --> 10:56.310
Of course.

10:56.310 --> 10:58.970
Could I borrow a pen?

11:00.280 --> 11:03.120
As long as you don't try 
anything funny with it.

11:06.780 --> 11:08.280
What are you doing?!

11:08.770 --> 11:12.780
This is necessary to draw out 
the relic's true potential.

11:13.160 --> 11:14.780
Let him do his thing, John.

11:15.120 --> 11:18.280
Don't make me regret 
giving you free rein, Goriki.

11:19.070 --> 11:20.780
Just watch.

11:24.620 --> 11:26.290
What are you writing?

11:26.290 --> 11:29.790
Tomb glyphs—the language of relics.

11:30.130 --> 11:34.000
Oh? You can use the language of relics, eh?

11:35.870 --> 11:39.640
With these incantations, 
the relics will display their talents.

11:41.670 --> 11:46.260
<i>Of course, this has nothing to do with 
finding the British prime minister.</i>

11:46.260 --> 11:51.020
<i>I located him in advance 
with Zheng He's treasure map.</i>

11:51.480 --> 11:54.150
Found him. The prime minister 
is in the Sahara Desert.

11:54.150 --> 11:55.400
What?

11:58.970 --> 12:02.770
Contact the nearest base to this location.

12:02.770 --> 12:05.870
I authorize the use of relics 
to expedite the search.

12:05.870 --> 12:07.180
Yes, ma'am!

12:07.180 --> 12:09.330
Since I've now kept my promi—

12:12.880 --> 12:18.060
You will not move from this spot until 
the prime minister has been found.

12:18.620 --> 12:21.890
What? But we don't know 
how long that'll take!

12:22.360 --> 12:25.390
Didn't you say you wanted 
to continue negotiating?

12:29.090 --> 12:30.400
I suppose I have no choice.

12:37.360 --> 12:39.730
General, we've found 
Prime Minister Albert.

12:39.730 --> 12:41.940
Good. Is he safe?

12:41.940 --> 12:46.200
Yes. He's exhausted, 
but his life isn't in danger.

12:46.200 --> 12:49.020
What a relief. Then I'll be—

12:49.020 --> 12:50.200
Hold it.

12:52.420 --> 12:54.370
Don't move.

12:54.370 --> 12:55.980
General.

12:55.980 --> 12:58.880
It seems you never intended to let us go.

12:59.210 --> 13:03.380
That power you have strikes 
me as rather dangerous.

13:03.380 --> 13:05.750
Very perceptive of you.

13:05.750 --> 13:07.390
A bit too late, though.

13:07.390 --> 13:08.470
What?

13:12.360 --> 13:14.180
What is going on?!

13:15.670 --> 13:17.190
My maps are burning!

13:17.190 --> 13:18.350
Put it out!

13:19.140 --> 13:20.460
I'm on it!

13:29.400 --> 13:30.220
Stop!

13:30.220 --> 13:31.750
What are you doing, you idiot?!

13:32.750 --> 13:34.000
What are you playing at?!

13:35.250 --> 13:36.700
Goriki, you...

13:38.210 --> 13:40.710
They're gone. Both of them.

13:43.350 --> 13:45.790
He'll pay for tricking me.

13:49.150 --> 13:50.730
What the heck?

13:54.210 --> 13:56.730
Phew. We actually made it out.

13:56.730 --> 14:01.110
Yeah. We're soaking wet now, 
but at least the mission succeeded.

14:01.820 --> 14:04.790
<i>Right after the explosion, 
Kotaro used the confusion</i>

14:04.790 --> 14:07.950
<i>to draw this fountain 
on the floor with his ink.</i>

14:07.950 --> 14:13.200
MONTMARTRE PAINTER'S INK
(GRADE B - RARE / CONSUMABLE RELIC)
USES: (49/100)

14:08.750 --> 14:11.240
<i>It used to belong to Ogawara's lawyer.</i>

14:11.240 --> 14:15.200
<i>It was a pain to use, so I'm glad 
I have an artist on my side now.</i>

14:16.360 --> 14:18.830
How did you cause that explosion?

14:19.680 --> 14:21.560
That was easy.

14:22.210 --> 14:24.030
I made Shakespeare's Pen

14:24.030 --> 14:27.690
look exactly like the general's 
pen and switched them.

14:28.710 --> 14:32.030
Then I wrote orders for a 
terrorist attack on the map.

14:31.130 --> 14:32.930
What is going on?!

14:32.930 --> 14:37.590
For that, I had memorized the names 
of several employees beforehand.

14:37.590 --> 14:40.480
Those names were among 
the tomb glyphs I wrote.

14:41.350 --> 14:47.060
When the order was activated, extreme 
stress drove Jamie to make the attack.

14:47.860 --> 14:52.690
John, on the other hand, 
saw an evil spirit on the map.

14:54.920 --> 14:57.620
The general won't be able 
to track us anymore.

14:57.620 --> 14:59.960
So let's head for Turkey.

15:01.420 --> 15:03.120
W-Wait for me!

15:13.360 --> 15:15.640
It's been a while, Jean Richard.

15:16.020 --> 15:18.420
My relics were damaged.

15:18.420 --> 15:22.690
I'm heading back to the US. I'll need 
a restorer immediately once I'm there.

15:23.210 --> 15:25.680
<i>Restoration jobs are piling up.</i>

15:25.680 --> 15:29.820
<i>TKBM just made the same kind of request.</i>

15:30.760 --> 15:35.210
I suspect the guy who came to me
was also involved in TKBM's case.

15:36.160 --> 15:39.210
He'll become a problem 
if we leave him unchecked.

15:39.210 --> 15:42.460
<i>I understand. But please don't worry.</i>

15:42.460 --> 15:45.190
<i>Pandora will soon be established,</i>

15:45.190 --> 15:50.740
<i>and we'll make sure ordinary people 
can no longer own or use relics.</i>

16:05.800 --> 16:07.770
The tomb is still there?

16:07.770 --> 16:11.990
But it should have belonged 
to the misfortune relic.

16:12.760 --> 16:16.640
Once the relic attached itself to 
Irene-san, it should have disappeared.

16:17.590 --> 16:20.080
Part of the tomb has collapsed.

16:21.010 --> 16:22.920
There are a lot of people there.

16:24.090 --> 16:27.300
That's the American Tomb 
Special Operations Force.

16:27.300 --> 16:30.060
And those look like 
Turkish soldiers over there.

16:30.060 --> 16:32.260
Apparently, they're working together.

16:32.660 --> 16:36.770
Not even an ant could sneak past them.

16:37.160 --> 16:38.770
What do we do now?

16:38.770 --> 16:41.420
We still have a way. Follow me.

16:46.630 --> 16:50.180
Normally, a tomb is protected 
by the relic's aura.

16:51.010 --> 16:53.030
The direct entrance is blocked to us,

16:55.360 --> 16:58.040
but with this, we can still get inside.

16:58.590 --> 17:00.140
Hm? What is that?

17:00.140 --> 17:02.490
How are you going to use a sweet potato?

17:02.490 --> 17:05.400
It belonged to the little girl 
from the American squad.

17:06.050 --> 17:09.550
The Brother's Sweet Potato. 
It causes gas.

17:10.080 --> 17:12.550
That ain't gonna do shit for us!

17:12.900 --> 17:15.890
But in this situation, 
it will be most useful.

17:19.390 --> 17:21.690
What do you think you're doing?!

17:21.070 --> 17:23.690
Okay, potato, explode already.

17:21.690 --> 17:25.340
It's hot! Too hot! I'm burning!

17:23.690 --> 17:25.690
I need your energy.

17:26.570 --> 17:27.920
Why are you doing this?!

17:27.920 --> 17:31.200
Ow! It hurts! I'm going to explode!

17:32.140 --> 17:32.960
What was that?

17:32.960 --> 17:34.310
An explosion in the cave!

17:34.310 --> 17:36.040
Hurry! Move!

17:48.720 --> 17:50.530
Did you find something?

17:51.040 --> 17:54.090
This is the tomb of the Hand of Midas.

17:54.470 --> 17:55.940
"Midas"?

17:55.940 --> 17:59.420
Didn't everything he touched turn to gold?

17:59.420 --> 18:02.700
That makes no sense. 
She's already plagued by bad luck.

18:02.700 --> 18:06.020
The golden hand ultimately 
becomes the hand of misfortune.

18:06.020 --> 18:07.880
That's how the story ends.

18:09.640 --> 18:15.610
<i>The wine god Dionysus once gave 
gold-obsessed King Midas a golden hand.</i>

18:15.610 --> 18:18.900
<i>Any food he touched with it 
turned to gold at once,</i>

18:18.900 --> 18:21.060
<i>leaving Midas at risk of starvation.</i>

18:21.920 --> 18:25.960
<i>Dionysus explained that 
he had to give up the gold</i>

18:25.960 --> 18:30.890
<i>and bathe in the Pactolus River 
to turn his hand back to normal.</i>

18:33.520 --> 18:36.120
<i>Right. The Pactolus River.</i>

18:48.420 --> 18:49.730
Here it is.

18:53.740 --> 18:56.040
A lake this huge underground?

18:56.990 --> 19:01.540
Midas bathed in the river to 
rid himself of his golden hand.

19:01.540 --> 19:04.330
The same might work with your relic.

19:07.920 --> 19:10.090
There doesn't seem to be a trap.

19:10.090 --> 19:12.590
Then what should I do?

19:13.600 --> 19:15.750
Well...

19:22.220 --> 19:24.020
You don't mean...

19:42.490 --> 19:46.000
Boss, is it necessary to watch her like that?

19:46.410 --> 19:47.870
You said there aren't any traps.

19:47.870 --> 19:50.000
I'm just making sure.

19:50.410 --> 19:53.670
A rejected relic can 
quickly become fickle.

19:56.450 --> 19:58.950
I wonder if this will really help.

20:03.380 --> 20:04.390
Search everything!

20:04.950 --> 20:06.770
This way! Hurry!

20:08.530 --> 20:10.730
Boss! The soldiers are here!

20:11.010 --> 20:12.270
Keep an eye on Irene.

20:12.270 --> 20:16.110
What? B-But how am I supposed to... Wait!

20:20.440 --> 20:24.130
<i>Calm down, Kotaro. 
Why is my heart racing?</i>

20:27.120 --> 20:29.120
<i>It's fine. This isn't peeping.</i>

20:29.120 --> 20:31.960
<i>I'm only doing this to protect Irene-san!</i>

20:34.590 --> 20:35.630
Hey!

20:34.590 --> 20:35.630
Ow!

20:37.480 --> 20:40.060
B-Boss! You're back so soon...

20:40.060 --> 20:42.640
Um, I mean... Wh-What about the soldiers?

20:42.990 --> 20:46.140
They were all small fry.
I took care of them.

20:50.730 --> 20:52.130
Whoa.

20:54.090 --> 20:57.860
Maybe the method was too simple after all.

21:01.840 --> 21:05.950
At last, my other half has returned!

21:07.750 --> 21:08.790
A RELIC SLEEPING IN THE LAKE HAS AWAKENED.

21:07.750 --> 21:09.750
Hey, what now?

21:08.790 --> 21:09.750
THE GOLDEN RELIC IS EMITTING AN OMINOUS AURA.

21:09.750 --> 21:11.250
WARNING
IMMENSE LUCK IS FLOWING TOWARD YOU.
LUCK OF THIS MAGNITUDE MAY BRING GREAT DANGER.

21:11.870 --> 21:12.960
Damn it!

21:13.690 --> 21:15.180
Get out of there!

21:15.180 --> 21:18.890
I can't control my body! Ryoga-san!

21:20.180 --> 21:21.380
What's happening?!

21:21.380 --> 21:22.300
Shit!

21:23.140 --> 21:24.350
Why is this happening?

21:25.510 --> 21:27.840
Think! Think of something now!
